# A left-associative chain of N additions is a tree N levels deep, from
# input of 2N+1 bytes. Printing it (`Sexp.write`) and taking its span (the
# hull of a list without a node id) keep their stack on the heap: with
# N = 1,000,000 a walk that recursed on the native stack would overflow it.
#
# The case file holds N; the lang module's Parser builds the input
# `x+x+...+x`, parses it, walks the tree, and returns a summary string.

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    plus
    eof
    err
'+'                                         → plus
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "deep_tree"

prog! = sum                                 → (prog 1)
sum   = sum "+" IDENT                       → (1 3)
      | IDENT
